## Done Means

- Validate the affected behavior with focused checks. Run broader suites when shared behavior, failures, or unresolved risks warrant them.
- Once the affected behavior is verified, finish; repeat checks only for changed inputs or a concrete remaining concern.
[% if frontend_apps | length > 0 %]
- For frontend changes, select the relevant `scripts/jig check typescript-*` checks.
[% endif %]
[% if sqlx_enabled %]
- For SQLx or migration changes, run `scripts/jig check sqlx`.
[% if schema_dump_enabled %]
- For schema or schema-documentation changes, run `scripts/jig check schema`.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
- Review the generated diff for stale docs, policy drift, or missing dependent updates.

## [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]Crate Guide[% else %]Backend Guide[% endif %] Conventions

When a [% if rust_workspace_guidance_enabled %]Rust crate[% else %]backend package or crate[% endif %] has an `AGENTS.md`, [% if _jig.contract_version >= 9 %]these sections are optional suggestions:[% else %]use these sections:[% endif %]

- `## Purpose`
- `## Key entrypoints`
- `## Edit here for X`
- `## Invariants`
- `## Common commands`
[% if _jig.contract_version >= 9 %]
Use the structure that fits the area. Preserve ownership, entrypoints, invariants, and useful commands. Link to repository files when a reference must be checked. Run `scripts/jig check agent-guides` to validate local links and explicitly declared component guidance.
[% endif %]
